WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.090
Freya Allan's role as Princess Ciri on Netflix's
original series The Witcher is undoubtedly

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.840
the breakout moment of her career.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.680
At only 18 years old, Allan's only just getting
started, but she already had some extraordinarily

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.280
good luck even before landing this major gig.

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:20.920
Born in Oxfordshire, England in 2001, Allan
told Digital Spy that she underwent a confusing

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:26.060
audition process for The Witcher, as she didn't
really know she was auditioning to portray

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.580
Ciri, and initially thought she landed a smaller
part.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.280
Now that she's settled into the starring role,
she's apparently beloved by the production

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:32.780
team.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.700
Director Marc Jobst took a moment to lavish
her with praise in a quick question-and-answer

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:44.050
session on twitter, describing her portrayal
of Ciri as, quote, "luminous...fierce, charismatic,

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.060
with the presence and strength of an old soul."

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.540
"Nothing for you to be concerned about."

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.300
"Your dismissive tone says it is."

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.760
Allan's screen presence is indeed powerful,
and many of you Witcher watchers at home have

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.980
probably scratched your head and wondered
where you've seen the actress before.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.920
While her career has only just taken off in
the past year, Allan may look familiar to

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:07.420
many.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:12.860
After attending the same prestigious academy
as Harry Potter franchise icon Emma Watson,

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:18.070
the Headington School in Oxford, Allan began
her artistic secondary education at the prestigious

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.180
National Film and Television School in Buckinghamshire.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.740
From there, Allan went on to study at the
Art University Bournemouth and starred in

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.720
a short film called Captain Fierce.

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:32.760
In the short, Allan plays Linda, a girl who
can only meet up with her friend Danny once

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.300
a year because her family is part of a traveling
carnival.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:40.020
They find an abandoned, damaged boat and decide
to fix it so they can run off together.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.490
The short appears to have been uploaded to
YouTube as part of the hype building up around

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:49.000
The Witcher's casting announcements, as many
comments on the video speak positively about

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.660
Allan's pending role as Ciri.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:56.420
Before being taken under the wing of Henry
Cavill's Geralt of Rivia on The Witcher, Allan's

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:01.490
first big role was as a younger version of
martial arts expert Minerva, a major character

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.160
on AMC's action series Into the Badlands.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.179
The single episode in which Allan appeared
includes a flashback to when a teenage Minerva

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:13.060
was enslaved by one of the show's post-apocalyptic
Barons.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.280
Following her short stint on Into the Badlands,
she landed a small role on an installment

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:23.700
of the BBC's 2019 miniseries adaptation of
the beloved sci-fi novel War of the Worlds.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.620
Going from those roles to standing front and
center as part of The Witcher's major character

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.209
triad is one heck of a quantum leap, but that
momentum is here to stay for at least the

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:34.140
next couple of years.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.440
The Witcher was greenlit for a second season
even before all eight episodes went live on

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.980
Netflix, so that's a great sure thing for
Allan's future.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:46.360
However, Allan's early career renaissance
doesn't stop there.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:51.530
In 2020, Freya Allan will make her feature
film debut in the action thriller Gunpowder

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:52.040
Milkshake.

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:56.800
Details on the plot of Gunpowder Milkshake
are still slim, and there's no trailer just

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.950
yet, but Allan will once again play a younger
counterpart of the protagonist, in this case,

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.680
Karen Gillan's lead character Eva.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:09.880
Gillan will co-star alongside Game of Thrones
alum Lena Headey as a mother-daughter assassin

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.980
duo out to end the head of a gang for whom
they used to kill.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:17.800
Another woman-in-training for the warrior
class should feel nice and familiar for Allan

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:18.480
now, right?

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:23.680
Here's hoping Allan will be a fresh new leader
on the upward swing of this trend of female-led

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.620
original action films.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:30.129
Allan's other project, which is still in pre-production,
is a British program for Sky Media's new foray

00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:36.579
into original programming: a six-episode miniseries
entitled The Third Day, which is about residents

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.560
of a mysterious island who are set on preserving
their traditions at any cost.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:45.680
Of all the actress' forthcoming offerings,
The Witcher season 2 is the furthest out,

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:50.600
and we're sure she'll land a few more high-profile
gigs in the meantime, following her star-making

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.100
turn.

